+# H07 export audit
+
+Reviewed checkout `3078ede` against finding 2089 and R3 D4/D11. The shared checkout contains concurrent work. Evidence below comes from source inspection. Each slice has its own approval gate.
+
+## 2089 · Destination and existing exports
+
+- The desktop runs the CLI command table in-process. Both **Show in folder** buttons call `wb docs reveal`. Thread and page Make, document status/list, preview, update, open, reveal and delete use the CLI's `out_dir`. The `--open` branches and `docs open` also reconstruct the path themselves. [Desktop dispatch](../../../app/src-tauri/src/main.rs#L136) · [CLI](../../../crates/wb-cli/src/docs.rs#L19) · [Made dialog](../../../ui/src/pagedocs.ts#L223) · [Preview pane](../../../ui/src/pagedocs.ts#L273)
+- `WB_DOCS_DIR` currently wins. For the canonical real study directory, the resolver then uses `BIBLE_WORKBENCH_PDF_DIR` or `Documents/Bible Workbench`. Scratch studies default to a sibling named `<study>-documents`. The records in `<study>/documents/<id>.json` hold a filename and may hold a PDF companion, kept versions, a file hash and a signature. Status, update, preview and reveal all join the record's filename to the selected directory. A default-only change could mark existing files missing or make a same-named file in the new directory appear to belong to a legacy record. [Resolver and records](../../../crates/wb-core/src/docs/mod.rs#L48) · [Status](../../../crates/wb-core/src/docs/mod.rs#L220) · [Build](../../../crates/wb-core/src/docs/mod.rs#L401) · [Preview and reveal](../../../crates/wb-core/src/docs/mod.rs#L765)
+- Python also reads records from the study's `documents/` directory. It checks for files under one configured output directory, including companions and kept versions. Python's current source therefore cannot resolve a mixture of legacy and study-local exports through the same configuration. [Python records and status](../../../../bible-workbench/workbench/documents.py#L34) · [Python directory default](../../../../bible-workbench/workbench/pdf_export.py#L30)
+
+**Approve the destination and compatibility policy before coding.** Use `WB_DOCS_DIR` when explicitly set for new exports and `<study>/exports/` otherwise, including scratch. Keep JSON records under `<study>/documents/`. Use `BIBLE_WORKBENCH_PDF_DIR` or its historical default only to find older real-study exports. For older scratch records, allow lookup in that study's former sibling directory. Give new records location information that distinguishes study-relative exports from explicit overrides. If an override export cannot be located later, surface the missing location and let the user restore the configuration or explicitly reassign it. Confirm the record field and how an override location can be represented before implementation.
+
+Resolve existing records once for all commands. For legacy records, check the applicable directories and use the recorded hash to distinguish same-name candidates where possible. Surface ambiguous matches before any write or delete. A sole candidate with a changed hash should retain the edited-file safeguards. Apply the chosen directory consistently to companions and kept copies. Update or Make again should write at the resolved location and preserve edited versions, including on rename. If a file is missing, require an explicit destination choice where its former location cannot be determined safely. Keep relocation as a separate user action. Confirm whether Python must keep opening *new* Rust exports during the transition. If so, keep a shared configured destination or approve a coordinated Python resolver change before switching the default. [Build and edit preservation](../../../crates/wb-core/src/docs/mod.rs#L411) · [Delete](../../../crates/wb-core/src/docs/mod.rs#L595)
+
+## D4 · Parts builder
+
+- The page Make flow already obtains rows with `wb craft parts --page`, shows **What goes in**, and sends the same row keys through `--on` and `--off` on Make. Core stores deviations from row defaults and uses those keys to select blocks in source order. To-dos and word blocks default off. The page title is always included in the source, and each immediate child is one switch. Threads use a separate source path. [Page Make](../../../ui/src/pagedocs.ts#L142) · [Switch handling](../../../crates/wb-core/src/docs/mod.rs#L699) · [Row defaults and keys](../../../crates/wb-core/src/docs/page.rs#L199) · [Plan source](../../../crates/wb-core/src/docs/page.rs#L395) · [Thread source](../../../crates/wb-core/src/docs/mod.rs#L175)
+- The page Adjust panel currently asks for `docs plan --page` with the format alone. The core uses the saved choices for that format's default structure. A new live preview could therefore disagree with the pending switches, version or structure unless it takes the same inputs as Make. The thread Adjust flow already passes its selected structure. [Page Adjust](../../../ui/src/pagedocs.ts#L123) · [CLI plan command](../../../crates/wb-cli/src/docs.rs#L126) · [Page plan](../../../crates/wb-core/src/docs/mod.rs#L752) · [Thread Adjust](../../../ui/src/documents.ts#L148)
+
+**Approve a first slice based on page rows.** Reuse the existing switches behind **What goes in** with the source order and make the live preview use the same pending choices as Make. Keep the existing CLI switch behavior and shipped structures. Confirm whether D4's thread-wide switches, title and styling controls, drag reorder, and named template persistence belong in a later slice. For any scripture inclusion switch, the selected source blocks define what must appear verbatim. Derive that expected set independently of the rendered plan so a renderer or planner omission still fails the check. [D4 design](../../redesign-R3.md#L219) · [Source verse checks](../../../crates/wb-core/src/docs/mod.rs#L345)
+
+## D11 · Page count and ink
+
+- Typst already returns the laid-out PDF page count and the record stores it as `pages`. Page Make shows that count, and the finished PDF preview counts its SVG pages. Word's finished preview reads the document's paragraphs into one scrolling sheet, while Adjust uses a styled sample. Neither yields Word's page breaks. The Ink setting changes styles. D11's light/moderate/heavy figure requires measuring darkness-weighted coverage from laid-out pages. [Typst render](../../../crates/wb-core/src/docs/deck.rs#L273) · [PDF record](../../../crates/wb-core/src/docs/mod.rs#L476) · [Finished previews](../../../ui/src/pagedocs.ts#L273) · [Adjust sample](../../../ui/src/looks.ts#L126) · [D11 design](../../redesign-R3.md#L312)
+
+**Approve the page-count and measurement scope.** Start with the actual Typst page count for PDF using the same plan and layout settings as Make. For an existing stale or edited PDF, distinguish a last-built count from a count verified from the current file. Leave Word pagination unavailable initially, or explicitly approve an **Estimated pages** figure with a defined paginated renderer and verification cases. Confirm the output formats, page coverage method, thresholds and print treatment of dark slides before adding ink labels. Keep W-5 with the user for real Word and PDF, including Word on a machine without the bundled fonts. [Prior W-5 status](../../phase2-results.md#L1038)
+
+## Acceptance after approval
+
+| Slice | Checks to run on isolated fixtures |
+| --- | --- |
+| 2089 | Exercise default, override, legacy configured and fallback paths using a stand-in for real-study detection and a separate scratch study. Test old records without location data, edited files, companions, kept versions, same-name conflicts, missing files and override changes. Check Make and Make again, list/show, preview, update including `--open`, open/reveal and delete against the resolved path. Verify no implicit relocation and no changes to the real study or its exports. |
+| D4 | Compare UI and CLI preview/build for default, off/on, mixed version, nested and reopened records. Verify source order, saved choices and expected scripture inclusion. Run `python scripts/doc-plans.py` for unchanged Speaker Script and Verse by Verse fingerprints against Python. Keep the missing-verse rejection check and compare rendered fixture verses against database text. |
+| D11 | Match preview PDF count to generated file count for short and overflowing layouts. Verify unavailable or estimated Word text according to the approved decision. If ink ships, use fixtures with known coverage and show the result changing between supported print styles. |
+
+**This pass.** Source inspection and document review only. Rust, desktop, Python compatibility, document-plan and rendered-verse checks were unrun in this audit. The merged desktop **420/420**, earlier plan **14/14**, and focused R3 desktop **9/9** are recorded results from other runs. This review is the sole H07 file added. [Recorded checks](../../phase2-results.md#L996) · [R3 and merged checks](../../phase2-results.md#L1104)
+
+- **Aligns with your request.** Separates path handling from presentation, uses existing parts switches and PDF layout, preserves plan and verse checks, and leaves W-5 with you.
